-- ADAPTER NOTES (approval/policy, per the integrator order) --
- wait_timeout is NOT in std Rust: implement by poll-waiting with child.try_wait() in a loop
  (std::thread::sleep 50 ms steps up to the deadline, then child.kill()) -- no new dependency.
- Endpoint/URL/data/limits/deny: same policy as the MCP diff notes above; one shared contract.
- Exit codes: 0 = text delivered; 3 = any refusal (the contract code is printed in the JSON).

